## AIM
To write a simple JavaScript program and test it using the Karate framework.

## THEORY

JavaScript is a programming language used for web development.

Karate is an open-source testing framework used for API testing and automation. It can execute JavaScript functions and verify their results using assertions.

In this experiment:
- A JavaScript function performs addition.
- A Karate feature file reads the JavaScript file.
- Karate executes the function with different inputs.
- Karate checks whether the actual result matches the expected result.

## STEP 1: Create Experiment 11 Folder

Open VS Code PowerShell and execute:

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\Dell\Desktop\external"

New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path "exp11"

cd "exp11"
```

## STEP 2: Create Project Folders

```powershell
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path "src\test\java\examples\demo"

